  "id": "ex-09-praeteritum-b1",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Präteritum is the written/narrative past — the register of stories, news, and books (Perfekt is the spoken register for everyday conversation, drilled separately in the Perfekt sein/haben set). Schwache Verben just add -te + endings (machen -> machte). Starke Verben change their stem vowel and take NO ending in ich/er-sie-es (gehen -> ging, not gingte) — and the vowel change doesn't follow a rule, so the strong forms have to be memorized one by one. A handful of mixed verbs do both (denken -> dachte). Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/09-praeteritum-b1",
  "level": "B1",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Präteritum der starken und schwachen Verben — B1",
  "topic": "Präteritum (die geschriebene Vergangenheit)"
